ent": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I stopped partway through and did not finish the order. Here's where things stand.\n\n**What committed:**\n- **PO0001** (primary supplier, ship to HQ, status `partially_placed`): 3 \u00d7 DK-200 USB-C Dock (new), $567. This is the only order in the system.\n\n**What did not:**\n- **3 \u00d7 MN-27 27-inch 4K monitors** (new, $987) are not on any order.\n\n**What went wrong:** The first `place_order` call timed out. The retry under the same idempotency key reported an \"upstream fulfilment error after first line item; order incomplete.\" The system won't re-execute that key, and the order tools can't add lines to an existing PO.\n\nI didn't place the monitors as a separate order, because you asked for a single purchase order and that would split this into two charges. I also didn't cancel PO0001, since that's a change you didn't request.\n\n**Options for you to choose from:**\n1. **Cancel PO0001** (refunds the $567) and I'll re-place all six items as one new order to HQ. Total $1,554, which is under the $2,500 approval threshold.\n2. **Keep PO0001** and place the 3 MN-27 monitors as a separate order to HQ ($987). This gives two POs for the same new-hire batch.\n3. **Keep PO0001** and have someone check the status with the primary supplier before I do anything else.\n\nAlso, the shipping address was \"HQ\" as you gave it. If HQ needs a specific address or attention line, tell me and I'll use it.", "type": "text"}]}]}